  "hypotheses": [
    "A burst beyond the backpressure capacity is admitted up to capacity; every other occurrence is rejected with its depth and capacity, through both its admission result and the rejected-overload callback, before its operation runs, and is never drained later.",
    "Shutdown mid-burst stops admitting at once, drains within its deadline, and its report accounts for every admitted occurrence as completed or abandoned; submissions after shutdown starts are rejected while shutting down.",
    "On the best_effort path, every drop is reported with the saturating loss count, the loss-ceiling signal fires once at the configured ceiling, and the binding never claims a dropped occurrence was delivered.",
    "The accounting identity holds for every phase, with overload, shutdown and drop losses in the denominator and none unexplained."
  ],
